{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>One Shechem.</b> The alef with patach." "<b>Which I took.</b> Which I am destined to take in the days of Joshua, in wars of sword and bow — like ״I gave the price of the field,״ which is like ואתן (and I will give). And furthermore, it is important in Jacob's eyes as though he had already taken it, since HaShem promised it to him. And that he specified the Amorite and no other nation — because he was mightier than all of them, as it is written: ״And I destroyed the Amorite from before you, whose height was like the height of cedars, and strong as oaks.״ Another interpretation: of HaShem he speaks — <b>with my sword and with my bow</b> — like ״He is your help and the sword of your pride,״ [where the sword is HaShem]. Here Rashi explained: when Simeon and Levi killed the men of the city, all the surrounding peoples gathered to join battle with them, etc. — but they did not join battle, as it is written: ״and they did not pursue after the sons of Jacob.״"], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 48, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:09:07.580175203Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}